BFS gives shortest paths when edges are unweighted:

```python
from collections import deque

def shortest_path(graph, start, goal):
    q = deque([[start]])
    visited = {start}
    while q:
        path = q.popleft()
        node = path[-1]
        if node == goal:
            return path
        for nbr in graph[node]:
            if nbr not in visited:
                visited.add(nbr)
                q.append(path + [nbr])
    return None
```

